# Starting up LOS
#
# Everything below is now handled by a single command:
#
#     los gateway
#
# It starts the memory server, the action MCP server, any enabled
# channels, the cron daemon and the web app — in dependency order, with
# health checks and automatic restarts — and stops them all cleanly on
# Ctrl-C.
#
#     los status          what is running
#     los logs -f         follow every log
#     los config          change ports, channels, users
#     los doctor          check the installation
#
# The old manual sequence is kept here for reference and for debugging a
# single service in isolation.  Each one still honours its historical
# defaults when started by hand.


# --- Reference: starting services individually -------------------------

# Ollama (external; not managed by the gateway by default):
ollama serve

# Cron daemon:
cd /los/sys/loscron
python loscron.py

# Web app:
cd /los/sys
source ssl_venv/bin/activate
cd ssl_server
python app.py

# Memory MCP server:
python /los/sys/memory_mcp/memory_server.py

# Action MCP server:
python /los/sys/aicall_mcp/action_server.py

# WhatsApp channel (optional):
cd /los/sys/whatsapp_mcp
source whatsapp_venv/bin/activate
python whatsapp_server.py

# To start the WhatsApp channel with a visible browser (to scan the QR code):
#   los config    -> Channels -> WhatsApp -> headless: no
# or, by hand:
#WHATSAPP_HEADLESS=0 python whatsapp_server.py


# --- External agents ---------------------------------------------------

# Kick off openclaw:
openclaw gateway

# Kick off hermes:
hermes dashboard

